<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Pan</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>viewport context menu &gt; Pan</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">, by pressing</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift + T</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">, or by pressing</span> <span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pan</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button on the toolbar.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">When this mode is enabled, hold down the left mouse button and move the mouse on screen. This will translate the viewport left, right, up, and down. Exit</span> <span class="Mode">Pan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode by switching to another one </span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Mode</span><span lang="EN-GB">, or</span> <span class="Mode">Rotate</span><span lang="EN-GB">. This mode is not stored so when you open another window,</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode will be enabled.</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image075.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt="">Mouse pointer in</span> <span class="Mode">Pan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Using</span> <span class="Shortcut">Shift + Right mouse button</span> <span lang="EN-GB">or only</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Middle mouse button</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">it will always switch to</span> <span class="Mode">Pan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode. When the mouse button is released, KUBE will switch to the previous mode.</span> When in <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Pan</u></span> mode manipulations with the mouse are infinite. This means that if the mouse cursor exit from the screen it automatically appears at the opposite side of the screen if the mouse continue in the same direction.</p>
